/*  Series — `a series of … with (…)`, `range … to …`, `For each`, `item … of`, `the number of`,
    `Insert`, `Remove` and setting an item — over numbers, text and facts.

    ★ A series is SHARED, as in the language: `Define t as s` names the same series, so an insert
      through `t` is seen through `s`. In C it is a pointer to one growable array.

    ★ One C type per kind of element — `cser_number`, `cser_text`, `cser_fact` — written into every
      program, used or not; C says nothing about a helper nobody calls. A series of anything else
      waits for a later slice.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The kind of a series' elements, or "" when `kind` is no series.
    Bind text to element-of, given (the text kind):
        If kind starts with "series of ", return the characters from 11 to the end of kind.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// Whether a kind is one of the three a value can be on its own.
    Bind fact to is-scalar, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "number" or kind is "text" or kind is "fact".
    Done.

    /// Whether a series can hold a kind: one of the three, an object, or a series that could itself.
    Bind fact to is-element-kind, given (the text kind):
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "", return cast is-element-kind on (cast element-of on (kind)).
        If cast is-voidable on (kind), return cast is-element-kind on (cast voidable-inner on (kind)).
        Return cast is-scalar on (kind) or kind is "bits" or cast object-of on (kind) is not "" or cast is-union on (kind) or cast is-record on (kind)
            or cast is-map on (kind) or cast is-function on (kind).
    Done.

    /// Notes a series whose element is itself generated — a series, or a voidable — so its type is
    /// written with the generated ones, after what it holds. Kept as `held:<element>`, which no
    /// union or voidable entry can be mistaken for.
    Bind void to register-series unto emitter, given (the text element):
        Define entry as "held:{element}".
        If (the entry for entry in one's unions) is void:
            In one's unions, the entry for entry becomes true.
            Insert entry into one's union-order.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The element a `held:` entry names, or "" for any other entry.
    Bind text to held-element, given (the text entry):
        If entry starts with "held:", return the characters from 6 to the end of entry.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// The C name of the series type that holds a kind.
    Bind text to series-c-name, given (the text element):
        // A series of series is named for what it holds: `cser_cser_text`.
        If cast element-of on (element) is not "", return "cser_{cast series-c-name on (cast element-of on (element))}".
        If cast is-voidable on (element), return "cser_{cast voidable-c-name on (element)}".
        If cast is-union on (element), return "cser_{cast union-c-name on (element)}".
        If cast is-record on (element), return "cser_{cast record-c-name on (element)}".
        If cast is-map on (element), return "cser_{cast map-c-name on (element)}".
        // A series of axioms is its own type, so it prints them as `<axiom>`.
        If element starts with "axiom ", return "cser_ax_{cast function-c-name on (element)}".
        If cast is-function on (element), return "cser_{cast function-c-name on (element)}".
        Define object-name as cast object-of on (element).
        If object-name is not "", return "cser_obj_{cast c-ident on (object-name)}".
        Return "cser_{element}".
    Done.

    /// The C a series type and its helpers are, for elements of one kind.
    Bind text to c-series-helpers, given (the text element):
        Define held as cast c-type on (element).
        Define series-type as "{cast series-c-name on (element)}".
        Define written as cast write-call on (element, "s->data[i]").
        Define equal as cast c-equal on (element, "s->data[i]", "v").
        Define out as a chase.
        Insert "typedef struct {series-type}_s {series-type};\n" into out.
        Insert "struct {series-type}_s \{ {held}* data; int len; int cap; \};\n" into out.
        Insert "static {series-type}* {series-type}_new(void) \{ {series-type}* s = ({series-type}*)cufet_arena_alloc(sizeof({series-type})); s->data = NULL; s->len = 0; s->cap = 0; return s; \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static void {series-type}_ensure({series-type}* s) \{ if (s->len >= s->cap) \{ int nc = s->cap == 0 ? 4 : s->cap * 2; {held}* nd = ({held}*)cufet_arena_alloc((size_t)nc * sizeof({held})); if (s->len > 0) memcpy(nd, s->data, (size_t)s->len * sizeof({held})); s->data = nd; s->cap = nc; \} \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static {series-type}* {series-type}_append({series-type}* s, {held} v) \{ {series-type}_ensure(s); s->data[s->len++] = v; return s; \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static void {series-type}_prepend({series-type}* s, {held} v) \{ {series-type}_ensure(s); if (s->len > 0) memmove(s->data + 1, s->data, (size_t)s->len * sizeof({held})); s->data[0] = v; s->len++; \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static void {series-type}_insert_after({series-type}* s, int after, {held} v) \{ {series-type}_ensure(s); if (s->len > after) memmove(s->data + after + 1, s->data + after, (size_t)(s->len - after) * sizeof({held})); s->data[after] = v; s->len++; \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static void {series-type}_remove_at({series-type}* s, int index) \{ if (s->len - index - 1 > 0) memmove(s->data + index, s->data + index + 1, (size_t)(s->len - index - 1) * sizeof({held})); s->len--; \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static void {series-type}_remove_value({series-type}* s, {held} v) \{ for (int i = 0; i < s->len; i++) if ({equal}) \{ {series-type}_remove_at(s, i); return; \} \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static int {series-type}_eq({series-type}* a, {series-type}* b) \{ if (a->len != b->len) return 0; for (int i = 0; i < a->len; i++) if (!{cast c-equal on (element, "a->data[i]", "b->data[i]")}) return 0; return 1; \}\n" into out.
        Insert "static void {series-type}_write({series-type}* s) \{ fputs(\"(\", stdout); for (int i = 0; i < s->len; i++) \{ if (i > 0) fputs(\", \", stdout); {written}; \} fputs(\")\", stdout); \}\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// Every series type a program may use, and the range that makes a series of numbers.
    Bind text to c-series-prelude:
        Define out as a chase.
        For each element in a series of text with ("number", "text", "fact", "bits"), repeat:
            Insert cast c-series-helpers on (element) into out.
        Done.
        Insert "static cser_number* cser_number_range(CufetDec from, CufetDec to, CufetDec step, int line) \{\n" into out.
        Insert "    if (cufet_cmp(step, cufet_dec_from_ll(0)) <= 0) cufet_raise(cufet_msgf(\"the step in 'counting by' must be positive (line %d).\", line));\n" into out.
        Insert "    cser_number* s = cser_number_new();\n" into out.
        Insert "    for (CufetDec n = from; cufet_cmp(n, to) <= 0; n = cufet_add(n, step)) cser_number_append(s, n);\n" into out.
        Insert "    return s;\n\}\n\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// What a refusal calls the series it reaches into: its name, when it has one.
    Bind text to series-label, given (the node target):
        If target's kind is "VariableReference", return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)).
        Return "series".
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The kind a series expression gives, or a failure when it is beyond this compiler.
    Bind text or failure to series-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "SeriesLiteral":
            Define element as "void".
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) is false:
                The element becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            // `a series with (10, 20)` names no type — its items do.
            Otherwise if the number of (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children is greater than 0:
                The element becomes cast one's kind-of on (item 1 of (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            If cast is-element-kind on (element) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a series of {element}")).
            If cast element-of on (element) is not "" or cast is-voidable on (element), cast one's register-series on (element).
            Return "series of {element}".
        Done.
        If kind is "RangeExpression", return "series of number".
        If kind is "SeriesLength", return "number".
        // `item … of`, `the first of`, `the last of`.
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-record on (held), return cast one's record-item-kind on (held, cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        If held is "chase", return "text".
        Define element as cast element-of on (held).
        If element is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("an item of a {held}")).
        Return element.
    Done.

    /// A series expression as C.
    Bind text or failure to c-series-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "SeriesLiteral":
            Define element as cast element-of on (cast one's series-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off).
            Define series-c as cast series-c-name on (element).
            If the number of (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children is 0, return "{series-c}_new()".
            // One statement per item, so the items are worked out in the order they are written —
            // C leaves the order of a call's arguments open, and gcc takes them last first.
            Define built as "(\{ {series-c}* cf_sl = {series-c}_new();".
            For each written in (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children, repeat:
                The built becomes "{built} cf_sl = {series-c}_append(cf_sl, {cast one's c-of-as on (written, element) or pass the failure off});".
            Done.
            Return "{built} cf_sl; \})".
        Done.
        If kind is "RangeExpression":
            Define lowest as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define upto as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Define step as "cufet_dec_from_ll(1)".
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) is false:
                The step becomes cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Return "cser_number_range({lowest}, {upto}, {step}, {(cast field-of on (expression, 4))'s word})".
        Done.
        Define target as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define target-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "SeriesAccess" and cast is-record on (target-kind):
            Return cast one's c-record-item on (series-c, target-kind, cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesAccess" and target-kind is "chase":
            Return cast one's c-chase-item on (target, cast field-of on (expression, 2), (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define element as cast element-of on (target-kind).
        If kind is "SeriesLength", return "cufet_dec_from_ll(({series-c})->len)".
        // `item … of`: the series is held once, so it is reached once.
        Define at-line as (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word.
        Define place as cast one's c-place on (cast field-of on (expression, 2), "cf_at", target, at-line) or pass the failure off.
        Return "(\{ {cast series-c-name on (element)}* cf_at = {series-c}; cf_at->data[{place}]; \})".
    Done.

    /// The zero-based place of an item in the series `held` names in C — `_` for the last — checked
    /// against its length, as the language refuses an item that is not there.
    Bind text or failure to c-place unto emitter, given (the node index, the text held, the node target, the text at-line):
        If cast is-nothing on (index), return cast c-place-at on ("", held, target, at-line).
        Return cast c-place-at on (cast one's c-of on (index) or pass the failure off, held, target, at-line).
    Done.

    /// `c-place` with the index already as C — "" for the last.
    Bind text to c-place-at, given (the text index-c, the text held, the node target, the text at-line):
        Define label as cast series-label on (target).
        If index-c is "", return "cufet_last_check({held}->len, \"{label}\", {at-line}) - 1".
        Return "cufet_idx_check(cufet_to_int({index-c}), {held}->len, \"{label}\", {at-line}) - 1".
    Done.

    /// `<series> sorted`, `in reverse`, `by the <field>` — a new series, the old one left as it was.
    Bind text or failure to sorted-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If held is "chase", return "chase".
        If cast element-of on (held) is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("sorting a {held}")).
        Return held.
    Done.

    /// The function a sort is `by`, or nothing: a function written in place, or one named — which
    /// the tree also leaves in the field's place, beside a `:KeyFunction` saying what it is.
    Bind node to sort-key-function, given (the node expression):
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 6)) is false, return cast field-of on (expression, 6).
        Define place as 0.
        For each part in expression's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If part's word is ":KeyFunction", return item (place + 1) of expression's children.
        Done.
        Return cast field-of on (expression, 6).
    Done.

    /// The key a sort compares: the element, or its field.
    Bind text or failure to sort-key-kind unto emitter, given (the text element, the node by-field):
        If cast is-nothing on (by-field), return element.
        Define field-name as cast unquoted on (by-field).
        If cast is-record on (element), return cast record-field-kind on (element, field-name).
        If cast object-of on (element) is not "", return cast one's field-kind on (cast object-of on (element), field-name) or pass the failure off.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// A sort as C: a copy, put in order by a stable insertion sort — equal keys keep their order, as
    /// the interpreter's does. Numbers compare as numbers; text by its bytes, as `cufet build` has it.
    Bind text or failure to c-sorted unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define held as cast one's sorted-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define reversed as (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word is "true".
        If held is "chase":
            If reversed, return "cufet_chase_sorted({series-c}, 1)".
            Return "cufet_chase_sorted({series-c}, 0)".
        Done.
        Define element as cast element-of on (held).
        Define series-type as cast series-c-name on (element).
        Define key-function as cast sort-key-function on (expression).
        If cast is-nothing on (key-function) is false:
            Return cast one's c-sorted-by-function on (series-c, element, key-function, reversed) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define by-field as cast field-of on (expression, 2).
        Define key-kind as cast one's sort-key-kind on (element, by-field) or pass the failure off.
        Define left-key as "cf_dst->data[cf_j]".
        Define right-key as "cf_k".
        If cast is-nothing on (by-field) is false:
            Define member as cast c-name on (cast unquoted on (by-field)).
            The left-key becomes "(cf_dst->data[cf_j]).{member}".
            The right-key becomes "(cf_k).{member}".
        Done.
        Define compared as "".
        If key-kind is "number", the compared becomes "cufet_cmp({left-key}, {right-key})".
        Otherwise if key-kind is "text", the compared becomes "strcmp({left-key}, {right-key})".
        Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on ("sorting by a {key-kind}")).
        Define out-of-order as "({compared}) > 0".
        If reversed, the out-of-order becomes "({compared}) < 0".
        Return "(\{ {series-type}* cf_src = {series-c}; {series-type}* cf_dst = {series-type}_new(); for (int cf_i = 0; cf_i < cf_src->len; cf_i++) {series-type}_append(cf_dst, cf_src->data[cf_i]); for (int cf_a = 1; cf_a < cf_dst->len; cf_a++) \{ {cast c-type on (element)} cf_k = cf_dst->data[cf_a]; int cf_j = cf_a - 1; while (cf_j >= 0 && {out-of-order}) \{ cf_dst->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_dst->data[cf_j]; cf_j--; \} cf_dst->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_k; \} cf_dst; \})".
    Done.

    /// `<series> sorted by <function>` — the same stable sort, over keys worked out UP FRONT, each
    /// once and in order, as the interpreter does; they move with their items.
    Bind text or failure to c-sorted-by-function unto emitter, given (the text series-c, the text element,
            the node key-function, the fact reversed):
        Define function-kind as cast one's kind-of on (key-function) or pass the failure off.
        Define key-kind as cast function-gives on (function-kind).
        If key-kind is not "number" and key-kind is not "text", return a failure (cast not-built on ("sorting by a function giving a {key-kind}")).
        Define function-c as cast one's c-of on (key-function) or pass the failure off.
        Define compared as "strcmp(cf_keys->data[cf_j], cf_kk)".
        If key-kind is "number", the compared becomes "cufet_cmp(cf_keys->data[cf_j], cf_kk)".
        Define out-of-order as "({compared}) > 0".
        If reversed, the out-of-order becomes "({compared}) < 0".
        Define series-type as cast series-c-name on (element).
        Define keys-type as cast series-c-name on (key-kind).
        Return "(\{ {series-type}* cf_src = {series-c}; {series-type}* cf_dst = {series-type}_new(); {keys-type}* cf_keys = {keys-type}_new(); {cast function-c-name on (function-kind)} cf_kf = {function-c}; for (int cf_i = 0; cf_i < cf_src->len; cf_i++) \{ {series-type}_append(cf_dst, cf_src->data[cf_i]); {keys-type}_append(cf_keys, cf_kf.fn(cf_kf.env, cf_src->data[cf_i])); \} for (int cf_a = 1; cf_a < cf_dst->len; cf_a++) \{ {cast c-type on (element)} cf_k = cf_dst->data[cf_a]; {cast c-type on (key-kind)} cf_kk = cf_keys->data[cf_a]; int cf_j = cf_a - 1; while (cf_j >= 0 && {out-of-order}) \{ cf_dst->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_dst->data[cf_j]; cf_keys->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_keys->data[cf_j]; cf_j--; \} cf_dst->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_k; cf_keys->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_kk; \} cf_dst; \})".
    Done.

    // ── Statements ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The kind of a series' elements, for a statement that changes it.
    Bind text or failure to changed-element unto emitter, given (the node target):
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define element as cast element-of on (held).
        If element is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("changing a {held}")).
        Return element.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to emit-series-statement unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        If kind is "ForEachStatement":
            Cast one's emit-for-each on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesInsertStatement":
            Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
            If (cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off) is "chase":
                Cast one's emit-chase-insert on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            Define insert-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-set on (insert-kind):
                Cast one's emit-set-insert on (statement, insert-kind) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            Define element as cast one's changed-element on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define value as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 1), element) or pass the failure off.
            // The series, then the value, then the place, as the interpreter works them out.
            Define operands as a series of node with (target, cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
            Define sides as a series of text with (series-c, value).
            Define following as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
            If cast is-nothing on (following) is false:
                Insert following into operands.
                Define following-c as cast one's c-of on (following) or pass the failure off.
                Insert following-c into sides.
            Done.
            Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (operands, sides).
            Define series-type as cast series-c-name on (element).
            If (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word is "true":
                Cast one's line on (cast in-order-statement on (prefix, "{series-type}_prepend({item 1 of sides}, {item 2 of sides});")).
                Return.
            Done.
            If cast is-nothing on (following):
                Cast one's line on (cast in-order-statement on (prefix, "{series-type}_append({item 1 of sides}, {item 2 of sides});")).
                Return.
            Done.
            Cast one's line on (cast in-order-statement on (prefix, "{series-type}_insert_after({item 1 of sides}, cufet_to_int({item 3 of sides}), {item 2 of sides});")).
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesRemoveValueStatement":
            Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
            // `Remove <key> from <map>` is written the same way.
            Define target-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-map on (target-kind):
                Cast one's emit-map-remove on (statement, target-kind) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            If target-kind is "chase":
                Cast one's emit-chase-remove on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            Define element as cast one's changed-element on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define sides as cast one's c-fields-in-order on (statement, 1, 2) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's line on (cast in-order-statement on (item 1 of sides, "{cast series-c-name on (element)}_remove_value({item 2 of sides}, {item 3 of sides});")).
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesRemoveAtStatement":
            Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
            If (cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off) is "chase":
                Cast one's emit-chase-remove on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            Define element as cast one's changed-element on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define place as cast one's c-place on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), "cf_at", target,
                (cast field-of on (statement, 3))'s word) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's line on ("\{ {cast series-c-name on (element)}* cf_at = {series-c}; {cast series-c-name on (element)}_remove_at(cf_at, {place}); \}").
            Return.
        Done.
        // `The item … of … becomes …`.
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define set-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If set-kind is "chase":
            Cast one's emit-chase-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast is-record on (set-kind):
            If cast is-place on (target) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("setting a field of something that is not a name")).
            Define record-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define member as cast one's c-record-item on (record-c, set-kind, cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Define part-held as cast one's record-item-kind on (set-kind, cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's line on ("{member} = {cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), part-held) or pass the failure off};").
            Return.
        Done.
        Define element as cast one's changed-element on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define value as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), element) or pass the failure off.
        // The series, then the place, then the value — C leaves an assignment's two sides unordered.
        Define index as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define operands as a series of node with (target, cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Define sides as a series of text with (series-c, value).
        If cast is-nothing on (index) is false:
            Define index-c as cast one's c-of on (index) or pass the failure off.
            The operands becomes a series of node with (target, index, cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
            The sides becomes a series of text with (series-c, index-c, value).
        Done.
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (operands, sides).
        Define place as cast c-place-at on ("", "cf_at", target, (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word).
        If cast is-nothing on (index) is false:
            The place becomes cast c-place-at on (item 2 of sides, "cf_at", target, (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word).
        Done.
        Cast one's line on ("\{ {prefix}{cast series-c-name on (element)}* cf_at = {item 1 of sides}; cf_at->data[{place}] = {item (the number of sides) of sides}; \}").
    Done.

    /// `For each <name> in <series>, repeat:` — over the items there when it began, as in C#. The
    /// name, or `it`, holds each in turn and is gone when the loop ends.
    Bind void or failure to emit-for-each unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define named as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define name as "it".
        If cast is-nothing on (named) is false, the name becomes cast unquoted on (named).
        Define over as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (over) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-map on (held):
            Cast one's emit-map-for-each on (statement, held) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast is-set on (held):
            Cast one's emit-set-for-each on (statement, held) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If held is "chase":
            Cast one's emit-chase-for-each on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        Define element as cast element-of on (held).
        If element is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("looping over a {held}")).
        Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (over) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's line on ("\{").
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Cast one's line on ("{cast series-c-name on (element)}* cf_each = {series-c};").
        Cast one's line on ("int cf_each_n = cf_each->len;").
        // ⚠ Inserting into or removing from the series it loops over is refused while it runs —
        // checked before each pass and once more on the way out, which `Stop` leaves without, as
        // the interpreter does (GRAMMAR: "The for-each body cannot add or remove elements").
        Cast one's line on ("for (int cf_i = 0; ; cf_i++) \{").
        In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes element.
        Cast one's declared-here on (name).
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "        ".
        Cast one's line on ("if (cf_each->len != cf_each_n) cufet_raise(cufet_msgf(\"'{cast series-label on (over)}' was modified during a for-each loop on line {(cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word} — collect into a separate series, or use a While loop if you need to change it while looping.\"));").
        Cast one's line on ("if (cf_i >= cf_each_n) break;").
        Cast one's line on ("{cast c-type on (element)} {cast c-name on (name)} = cf_each->data[cf_i];").
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Define loop-kept as cast one's entering-loop.
        Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's leaving-loop on (loop-kept).
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        Cast one's line on ("\}").
    Done.
Done.
